 | `art/blender/a2-built.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/built.glb` | Slide, picnic table, fence, bridge, steps, firewood, the flower bed, a rowing boat | Made for this game in Blender, in code. The firewood's corners say where on its log they are and the bridge's concrete how it stands in the rain; the game draws the rings, cracks, bark, boards, holes and runs from that in code (`src/render/firewood.ts`, `src/render/concrete.ts`), with no texture |
 | `art/blender/a2-yard.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/yard.glb` | Billsta's woodshed with its winter's firewood (drawn as the stack's is, `src/render/firewood.ts`), the rowing boat turned over on its trestles under a tarp (its loose corner a part of its own), the mailbox, the garden furniture under a tarp, the swings at Flärkenbadet, and Olympia's two goals and its kit table | Made for this game in Blender, in code. No name, number or mark on the mailbox or anywhere else |
 | `art/blender/a2-buildings.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/buildings.glb` | Äventyr 2's buildings that were built in code: Själevad's church far down the lake in Stormens öga (eight white walls of boards and battens with corner pilasters and round-arched windows, the door under a pediment, a tent roof with standing seams, the lantern storey, the bell turret with its gables and the spire), the beaver's lodge of mud and gnawed sticks on Älven's bank, Olympia's store with its striped awning and its floodlight masts, and Billsta's wooden power poles with their street lamps and wires. The windows' glass is the game's own | Made for this game in Blender by `art/blender/a2-buildings.py` (8 November 2026): shapes built from numbers, colours painted on their corners, and each thing's own shade baked in with Blender's Cycles. No texture. The church is interpreted from the description of Själevad's church in `docs/aventyr-2-reference-study.md`, not from a photograph or a measured drawing; its spire ends in a plain gilded ball. No letter, numeral, crest or mark on anything. Nothing in it comes from anyone else. |
-| `art/blender/flarken.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/flarken.glb` | Flärkenbadet's diving tower on its raft (a steel lattice, a deck of planks with its rail, a lower deck behind, the ladder, the raft on its floats with old tyres and its chains), the two changing huts of round logs by the path (one with the doorway and rail of its sliding door), the small tarred hut, the giant chess on its gravel pad, the painted board with its smiling wooden sun (a lake, a ridge and a sun in plain shapes, no letter or mark), and the jetty's other leg with its floats, posts, rope and life ring | Made for this game in Blender by `art/blender/flarken.py`: shapes built from numbers, colours painted on their corners, and their own shade baked in with Blender's Cycles. No texture. The sawn ends of the huts' logs say where on their log they are, and the game draws their rings and cracks in code (`src/render/firewood.ts`). Built from the descriptions of the place in `docs/aventyr-2-overhaul.md`, not from a picture; no letter, numeral or mark. Nothing in it comes from anyone else. |
+| `art/blender/flarken.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/flarken.glb` | Flärkenbadet's diving tower on its raft (a steel lattice, a deck of planks with its rail, a lower deck behind, the ladder, the raft on its floats with old tyres and its chains), the two changing huts of round logs by the path (one with the doorway and rail of its sliding door), the small tarred hut, the giant chess on its gravel pad, the painted board with its smiling wooden sun (a lake, a ridge and a sun in plain shapes) and the place's name, Flärken, in white across its lake in the game's own Playpen Sans at Olov's decision (9 November 2026), the jetty's other leg with its floats, posts, rope and life ring, and the puzzle at the jetty's end: a round field stone of granite with a quartz vein and lichen, a thick piece of old pine bark with its plates and layers, and the broken ends of the jetty's planks at the gap | Made for this game in Blender by `art/blender/flarken.py`: shapes built from numbers, colours painted on their corners, and their own shade baked in with Blender's Cycles. No texture. The sawn ends of the huts' logs say where on their log they are, and the game draws their rings and cracks in code (`src/render/firewood.ts`). Built from the descriptions of the place in `docs/aventyr-2-overhaul.md`, not from a picture. The name's letters are Blender's setting of `public/fonts/playpen-sans-700-sv.woff2` (OFL, listed above); no other letter, numeral or mark. Nothing in it comes from anyone else. |
 | `art/blender/a2-room.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/room.glb` | Sofa, floor lamp, plant, table, chairs, the toy shelf with its toys, the doll at its foot and the doll's small yellow raincoat (Stormkvällen), and the great stone of the meeting | Made for this game in Blender, in code |
 | `art/blender/motion.py`, `src/render/motion-data.ts` | How the family, Mormor and Morfar move: each one's walk and run, how each stands (breathing, the weight from one leg to the other, a look about), going down on a knee and up again, and getting up from a chair and sitting down on one, as keyed curves | Keyed for this game in Blender by `art/blender/motion.py` (8 November 2026), from pose lists written for it, and sampled there into the game's table. No clip, motion capture or animation library, and nothing generated by an AI tool; nothing in it comes from anyone else. |
 | `art/procedural/bredbyn-landmarks.ts`, `art/procedural/bredbyn-street.ts`, `scripts/bake-bredbyn.mjs`, `art/blender/bredbyn-shade.py`, `art/baked/boot/bredbyn.glb` | Anundsjö church and its separate wooden bell tower, plus six varied distant street facades | Original procedural geometry and vertex colours authored in code for this game, exported with three's MIT-licensed GLTFExporter; then, as the build's second step, each building's soft shade is baked into its vertex colours with Blender's Cycles (ambient occlusion, its parts together on its ground) by `art/blender/bredbyn-shade.py`, and it is written by `scripts/bake/export.py`. No texture. Public photographs were inspected for architectural and landscape cues only. Their authors, dates, CC BY-SA licences, source URLs and hashes are recorded in [the reference manifest](docs/bredbyn-reference-sources.json) and [study](docs/bredbyn-reference-study.md). Photo originals remain outside git and game packs; no photograph, downloaded model, photographic texture, business mark or private likeness is embedded in these assets. Street facades are interpretations, not copies of named shops or a measured survey. |
